Evening sweep November 1 2026, fired at 21:00 MST eleven hours after the midday pass. The mcpservers.org /all read repeated the morning failure and confirmed the rule: the first fetch, cache-busted on the target URL, returned the counter at 18,732 with the same thirty slugs the midday pass had already dispositioned, and a second fetch cache-busted with a nanosecond stamp returned 18,883 with all thirty turned over, so a reader-proxy /all read that repeats the previous counter is a stale snapshot rather than a quiet page and two cache-busted reads are the only read that counts. The mcp.so recentServers block carried 30 cards with a date and the newest at 2026-11-02T01:54:34Z, so six sat above the midday stamp of 2026-11-01T13:11:50Z: brontide, cdphub, instatus, cve-now, sazabi and opsis-osint. The submission window #6551 to #6584 held 31 submissions and every one was read with its body rather than triaged from a title. Two arrivals were catalogued, and both are keyless surfaces where the free half is the product. Reg Monitoring MCP - https://mcp.regmonitoring.com/mcp answered initialize with HTTP 200 and issued an mcp-session-id header, reported serverInfo regmonitoring 0.2.0, and listed seven tools with schemas. get_stats returned 6,107 records published between 2011-06-28 and 2026-10-30 from 34 regulators across 20 jurisdictions, with 5,528 carrying an AI analysis, 974 a deadline date, 100 a parsed penalty amount, 6,106 a significance score and 3,932 an urgency flag. get_taxonomy counts what can be filtered on and warns that the values are exact and case-sensitive: United Kingdom 1,196, United States 996, France 690, Luxembourg 648, Australia 358, Ireland 322, Germany 296, European Union 295, United Arab Emirates 187, Singapore 183, Hong Kong 179, behind regulators FCA 797, AMF 690, CSSF 648, SEC 394, ASIC 358 and Central Bank of Ireland 322. search_updates returns a per-record shape with content_type (speech, final_rule, enforcement, regulatory_notice), a significance_score from 1 to 5, published_date, deadline_date, has_analysis, the source_url on the regulator's own domain and offset pagination, and list_deadlines answered 974 matching deadlines each with a deadline_type, a status, a confidence, the sentence the date was parsed from and a firm_types list such as Broker Dealer, Wealth Manager and Bank. It earns a guide against The Bot Wire, a pipe into US primary documents with no jurisdiction filter, no consultation calendar and no firm-type field, while here the non-US records outnumber the American ones and the firm-type filter is what turns a feed into a work queue. HeritageDeed MCP - https://heritagedeed.com/mcp/public answered initialize with HTTP 200 keyless, reported serverInfo heritagedeed 1.30.0 with websiteUrl heritagedeed.com/developers, and listed 58 tools. The split is the product: lookups are free, documents are ordered. list_coverage returned 43 counties grouped by state with their main cities plus the eight inclusions and four exclusions of a title search, naming title insurance, a title commitment, an attorney opinion of title, a survey, payoff balances and any document recorded before the county online index begins. flood_zone_lookup on a live address returned a parsed FEMA National Flood Hazard Layer result rather than a link, with mapped false, sfha false, category no_mapped_hazard, the caveat that the layer is also empty where FEMA has published no digital map, the insurance consequence and a disclaimer that it is screening rather than an official determination. property_tax_rates_by_state returned the Census ACS 2020-2024 period with a US effective rate of 0.94 percent, median real estate taxes of 3,119 dollars, a median home value of 332,700 dollars across 84,210,142 owner-occupied homes. Reports are 49 dollars for a title search in the covered counties, 29 for an Environmental Records Report at any US address and 49 for a Property Tax Appeal Evidence Pack, or 25 from a prepaid credit, with Pro at 39 a month, Pro Reports at 199 with ten reports a month and Property Watch at 9.99 a month per property, alongside a REST API v1 with batches of up to 50 orders, an Idempotency-Key header, signed webhooks and a white-label company name. It earns a guide because Hercules answers who owns what and who to call, and this answers what is recorded against the parcel, what the ground around it carries, what a sale nets and what a tax sale leaves behind, with the ordered report at the end, while Fonciq, UK Land Registry and Dutch Property Context are single-country and none of them orders a document. Held: instatus, the official status page vendor, on the uptime class carried by WatchCron, healthchecks-mcp, realuptime-mcp and hosttracker-mcp; cve-now on the vulnerability class Bot Wire covers with its CISA wire; opsis-osint on OpenOSINT; brontide as a game; sazabi on coding-agent observability; cdphub-com-mcp as CdpHub, an independent CDP integration directory with six keyless tools measured, held for a second look beside Jitsu which manages a CDP rather than comparing them; taskavel-com and www-seliee-si on OAuth 401 with protected-resource metadata, on the project-management and aggregator classes; docfig-com-api on MainBook and BankConv which already convert PDF bank statements with balance validation; markethq-ai on the Octolens and Buska buying-signal class; GatherHQ #6558 as the closest call, a business question turned into a research report from simulated interviews, held on the research class carried by User Intuition added October 28 with a recruited panel of four million real consumers and the synthetic-versus-real distinction recorded so a later pass can rule on whether the simulation is its own slice; Truo on the Kontoflux regional bank-sync precedent; DMD Costs on the regional legal trio Fermat 360, NyayAssist and PRIMAMCP; Starlecta on the saturated creator-discovery class and the regional test; Seonix on saturated SEO; PDFDispatch on Bannerify, url-to-pdf and FynePDF; NoneCap on the captcha class; Ahel on the Apify-actor pay-per-call distribution class; Cloud Alter Ego on the memory class; Kalshi Eye on the prediction-market data class. Two corrections rather than holds: Anclum #6581 is a directory of 9,500+ MCP servers, and SEO Audit #6571 is a resubmission of the already catalogued seo-audit-console-mcp. Three /all detail slugs, graphify-labs, omnicoder-dev and testchimp, returned the 404 shell with no content behind the slug, and six more were personal handle listings with no product surface. Counts: mcpservers.org /all proxy 30 unique slugs with the counter at 18,883 against 18,732 stale, mcp.so recentServers 30 cards with a date and the newest at 2026-11-02T01:54:34Z, issue window #6551 to #6584 with 31 submissions read with bodies, guide tree 1,080 server entries before this pass and 1,082 after, across 1,230 entries of which 1,228 pre-dated the two new directories. The five tracked listing surfaces were re-probed: mcpservers.org 200 on /servers/corpusiq-io through the reader proxy with the page title carrying CorpusIQ, Glama 200 on the /mcp/connectors/ route with CorpusIQ present, the official registry carrying io.corpusiq/multi-source-mcp at version 1.0.0 with the mcp2 remote and a description still reading 30+ business systems against 40+ on the site as a metadata drift still open, Smithery returning HTTP 500 on two attempts, a service-side error rather than a delisting and last confirmed live at midday, and mcp.so at 404 on all four direct slugs and still not listed with the paid route declined. One probe gotcha recorded: a cache buster on a mcpservers.org DETAIL page breaks the route and returns the 404 shell, so the buster belongs on /all only.
